  "nrasTlsRule": "near-gate-nvidia-tls-split (the maintainer 2026-11-06): an NVIDIA or TLS check that can't reach its server (network down, timeout, server error) is an outage: orange row, ask once. Malformed evidence from near.ai (an unreadable GPU evidence blob or TLS quote, a wrong-length key field, a bad fingerprint, missing TLS fields) and an unrecognised NVIDIA answer are evidence: red row, block. teemoon's own fault (it lost the request nonce, couldn't build the address) is orange, asks, and its detail is the approved line 'this check failed inside teemoon, so it proves nothing.'. class: outage | evidence | teemoon. Added 2026-11-06 (the maintainer via pm): an NRAS signing key missing from NVIDIA's key set after one refetch is an outage (rotation on NVIDIA's side); no captured server certificate is an outage; a captured certificate whose public key can't be read is evidence. A certificate with an unsupported key type would be teemoon's fault, but the fingerprint hashes the whole SubjectPublicKeyInfo whatever the key type, so that case does not arise. reasonLine (pm 2026-11-06): on a teemoon fault the degraded reason, the GPU row and the TLS row say the fault line itself, never \"(service unreachable)\" or \"could not complete\". unpublished+… vectors (TLA+ finding F1): an unpublished image exempts only itself from the gate; any other evidence still blocks and any other outage still asks.",
  "nrasTlsCases": [
    {"check": "nras", "case": "nras-unreachable", "class": "outage"},
    {"check": "nras", "case": "jwks-unreachable", "class": "outage"},
